---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Architecture & Zero-Data Guarantee – fastbgremove.com"
  description="Learn about our 100% client-side privacy architecture. We never collect, transmit, or store your photos."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8 sm:py-12 space-y-8">
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#76B900] bg-[#76B900]/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-[2px] border border-[#76B900]/30 font-semibold">
        <span>🔒</span> PRIVACY ARCHITECTURE
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">
        Privacy by Architecture: Zero Server Uploads
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-[#A7A7A7]">
        Last updated: September 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-[#A7A7A7] space-y-6">
      <section class="space-y-3 p-6 rounded-[2px] bg-white dark:bg-[#121214] border border-zinc-200 dark:border-[#232326] shadow-xs relative">
        <div class="absolute -top-[1px] -left-[1px] w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-[#76B900]"></div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">1. The Zero-Upload Guarantee</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          At fastbgremove.com, privacy is not just a policy—it is a technical guarantee enforced by code architecture. When you drop, paste, or select an image on this website, <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">the image is processed entirely inside your local web browser</strong> using WebAssembly and ONNX Runtime.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Your image pixels are never converted to HTTP requests, never sent to external APIs, and never written to remote disks or cloud buckets.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 p-6 rounded-[2px] bg-white dark:bg-[#121214] border border-zinc-200 dark:border-[#232326] shadow-xs relative">
        <div class="absolute -top-[1px] -left-[1px] w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-[#76B900]"></div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">2. Technical Verification (How to Inspect)</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          You do not need to take our word for it. You can independently verify that zero image data is transmitted:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li>Open your browser Developer Tools (F12 or right-click &gt; Inspect).</li>
          <li>Click on the <strong>Network</strong> tab and filter by <strong>Fetch/XHR</strong>.</li>
          <li>Drop an image into fastbgremove.com and let it process.</li>
          <li>Observe that no network payloads containing image buffers or data URLs are sent anywhere.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 p-6 rounded-[2px] bg-white dark:bg-[#121214] border border-zinc-200 dark:border-[#232326] shadow-xs relative">
        <div class="absolute -top-[1px] -left-[1px] w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-[#76B900]"></div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">3. Compliance with Privacy Regulations</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Because fastbgremove.com does not collect, process, or store personal data or biometric photographs on any server infrastructure:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">GDPR & UK GDPR:</strong> Compliant by design (data localization to user's hardware).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">HIPAA:</strong> Safe for medical documentation and patient records.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">NDAs & Corporate Security:</strong> Safe for proprietary prototypes, executive signatures, and internal identity photos.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 p-6 rounded-[2px] bg-white dark:bg-[#121214] border border-zinc-200 dark:border-[#232326] shadow-xs relative">
        <div class="absolute -top-[1px] -left-[1px] w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-[#76B900]"></div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">4. Local Browser Caching</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          The first time you process an image, your browser will download the compiled WebAssembly model weights (~20MB). These files are stored in your browser's local cache so that future background removals happen instantly, even when completely offline.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
